Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 04:51:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/32] v10 raccord r2 closure: floating-point option refusal
 stated as a contract, four out-of-contract channels declared, permanent
 contract gate

Adversarial re-verification of the repaired tree 210b9fc (2 October 2026): finding B2 is closed for options written
in clear, but the configure-time refusal was still bypassed, without refusal or warning, by three channels that
nothing declared out of contract, plus a minor one. Decision of the developer: the refusal is a defence in depth
against options written in clear in the judged sets, it cannot be complete against every way of altering code
generation. No channel is closed here; every statement is made true and the contract is pinned as declared.
No product code changes: comments only in src/ and cli/ (the 15 GCC binaries keep the sha256 of the final replay,
checked on the frozen extraction of this closure).
- cmake/fp_flags.cmake: header rewritten around nine statements E1 to E9: scope (defence in depth), judged token
  sets and only them, probed compile sets and what the probe reads, channel A (payload of a linker token under LTO:
  clang, -flto with -Wl,-plugin-opt=-fp-contract=fast, 64, 71 and 2 FMA instructions in tower, cluster and
  catalogue, 81 gates of 81 green), channel B (flag set by add_definitions from a project include or a parent
  project: -freciprocal-math under clang, -mno-ieee-fp under gcc), channel C (response or config file carrying
  -cl-single-precision-constant under clang: the factor 1 + 1e-10 of DWelzl::contains folded to 1), channel D,
  minor (-mdaz-ftz in a response file or crtfastmath.o at link under gcc: MXCSR 0x9fc0 at main), compile-time
  hypotheses of the certified filters (no FMA contraction for kMargin) valid under the contract only,
  -ffp-contract=off on every compile line and the #error carried by every unit but tests/unit/fault_preload.cpp.
  Code lines untouched.
- README.md and PASSATION.md: section "Contrat des options flottantes" with the same nine statements; rows
  "filtres flottants" and "Raccord R2" no longer say every spelling, tokens of each option set, the probe also
  sees a response file, #error in every unit; gate counts after the closure (84 under GCC and Clang, 82 under
  sanitizers). PASSATION.md: open item 6, not implemented: behavioural self-test of the floating arithmetic at run
  time in each unit that carries a certified filter (non-contracted product-sum, division against reciprocal,
  double constant, rounding mode, DAZ and FTZ), refusing with numeric_failure, a status to add; it changes product
  code and needs the full replay.
- CMakeLists.txt, docs/conception/ARCH_v2.md, cmake/fp_probe.cpp, headers of site_tree.cpp, tower.cpp, tower.hpp,
  fp_strict.hpp and types.hpp, headers of the fp gates and of the engraved campaign: same corrections, pointers
  to the contract.
- new gate mhgp10_regression_fp_contract (and _clang or _gnu), labels gate and regression, python, no build:
  statements read word for word in the three living documents, pointers, retracted over-claims absent; judged and
  probed sets read in the code of fp_flags.cmake and compared with the lists the statements name; one accepted
  case per out-of-contract channel replayed at configure level (the option must reach the written compile or link
  commands), refused twins written in clear and the seven spellings of finding B2; per-unit guard under
  -ffast-math (23 units of 24). Mutants killed by their family: documents, code, and mutated trees where a channel
  is closed, a refusal is left to the probe, the exempt unit gains the guard, the guard is not included, the
  contraction option is not set. Codes 0, 1, 2, 3; exact floors; same output under python3 -O.
  Lines: compilateur=GNU ... canaux=2/2 admis=4 refus=9 unites=23/24 mutants_tues=82/82 ; compilateur=Clang ...
  canaux=3/3 admis=5 refus=4 unites=23/24 mutants_tues=83/83. Closing a channel fails the gate until the
  documents change.
- receipts/raccord_r2_20260930/cloture/README.md: placeholder, completed by the receipts commit.

